  "prefLabel": "Bea 502.47 Residential use",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Bea 502.47 “Residential use” means lands, buildings, or structures or portions thereof used, or designed or intended for use as a home or residence of one or more individuals, and includes a single detached dwelling, a semi-detached dwelling, a multiple-unit dwelling, an apartment dwelling, or the residential portion of a mixed-use building or structure.\n\nSource. #14043, eff 8-8-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/bea500.html"
